#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
termpilot-wrap — termpilot wrapper, v2 (end-to-end encrypted).

Subcommands:
  generate-token   Generate a fresh 32-byte random token and save to keyring
                   (or ~/.config/termpilot/token chmod 600 with warning if no keyring).
                   Show the resulting token. Gated by sudo (anti-shoulder-surf).
  show-token       Show the stored token. Gated by sudo.
  help             Print usage.
  run              Spawn a command in a PTY and bridge it to a remote relay,
                   encrypting all traffic with the stored token. The command
                   can be any interactive program (bash, tmux, htop, ...).
                   This is what `termpilot` invokes.

The wrapper trusts:
  - The OS keyring (or a properly chmod'd token file).
  - sudo as a "user is at the keyboard" gate for token operations.
  - The PTY-spawned child process.

The wrapper does NOT trust:
  - The relay server. All metadata and content go ciphertext-only.
  - The network. HTTPS plus AES-256-GCM with AAD bound to (stream, sid, seq).

Run-mode threading:
  output_uploader     batches PTY bytes, encrypts, POSTs in chunked records.
  input_poller        long-polls for input records, decrypts, writes to PTY.
  heartbeat           keeps the session alive on the relay (15s).
"""
